WEBVTT

00:00:07.128 --> 00:00:10.719
A signup list must grow without losing its order.

00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:13.725
Its backing storage is an internal array.

00:00:13.725 --> 00:00:16.070
Logical size counts added names.

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:19.662
Capacity counts array positions, including unused

00:00:19.662 --> 00:00:20.028
ones.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:58.601
When storage is full, add allocates an array twice as

00:00:58.601 --> 00:00:58.947
long.

00:00:58.947 --> 00:01:02.618
It copies only the used names in order, then replaces

00:01:02.618 --> 00:01:04.141
the storage reference.

00:01:04.141 --> 00:01:06.773
Each array keeps its own fixed length.

00:01:06.773 --> 00:01:10.305
Finally, it stores the new name and increases size.

00:01:10.607 --> 00:01:13.371
Unused String positions start as null.

00:01:13.371 --> 00:01:17.154
The final loop reads only indexes below size, as get

00:01:17.154 --> 00:01:17.808
requires.

00:01:17.808 --> 00:01:21.518
Predict the three size and capacity reports and the

00:01:21.518 --> 00:01:23.482
order of names, then pause.

00:01:28.374 --> 00:01:31.607
The empty collection reports zero out of two.

00:01:31.607 --> 00:01:33.188
Two additions fill it.

00:01:33.188 --> 00:01:36.995
The third doubles capacity to four while size becomes

00:01:36.995 --> 00:01:37.426
three.

00:01:37.426 --> 00:01:39.941
Copying preserves Maya, Luis, Nora.

00:01:39.941 --> 00:01:42.599
The unused position is never printed.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:45.459
Add a fourth name before the Grown report.

00:01:45.459 --> 00:01:48.502
Predict its size, capacity, and printed order.

00:01:48.502 --> 00:01:51.214
Would this addition copy the array again?

00:01:51.214 --> 00:01:53.530
Explain using the growth condition.
